User: How do I double every number in an array?
Assistant: [1, 2, 3].map { |n| n * 2 }
# => [2, 4, 6]

User: How do I merge two hashes?
Assistant: { a: 1 }.merge(b: 2)
# => {a: 1, b: 2}

User: How do I count how many times each element appears in an array?
Assistant: ['a', 'b', 'a', 'c', 'a'].tally
# => {"a" => 3, "b" => 1, "c" => 1}

User: How do I group numbers into odd and even?
Assistant: (1..6).group_by(&:odd?)
# => {true => [1, 3, 5], false => [2, 4, 6]}

User: How do I define a class with a constructor?
Assistant: class Point
  attr_reader :x, :y

  def initialize(x, y)
    @x = x
    @y = y
  end
end

Point.new(1, 2).x
# => 1

User: How do I sort a hash by its values?
Assistant: { b: 2, a: 3, c: 1 }.sort_by { |_key, value| value }
# => [[:c, 1], [:b, 2], [:a, 3]]

User: How do I build an array of squares?
Assistant: 3.times.map { |i| i * i }
# => [0, 1, 4]
